---
// /terms — the project's terms of use, in clause form. Content is honest to
// what actually ships (MIT OSS, no paid tiers, no hosted obligation — see
// PRD §8 and CLAUDE.md's distribution model). Legal pages obey UIUX §7 like
// everything else: blame patterns, numbers over adjectives, no fear-mongering.
import LegalDoc from '../layouts/LegalDoc.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const clauses = [
  {
    id: 'acceptance',
    heading: 'Acceptance',
    blocks: [
      'VibeShield — the scanner binary, the GitHub Action, the pre-commit hook, the npm launcher, and every rules pack in this repository — is free, open-source software released under the MIT License. There is no contract to sign and no terms to click through to run it. By using the software you are agreeing that this page accurately describes what it does: a static analyzer that reads your files, pattern-matches them against public rules, and prints what it finds.',
      'The legal license text is the MIT license itself, reproduced at the bottom of this page and in the LICENSE file in the repository. Everything above the license line on this page is a plain-language guide to it — helpful, but not the operative text.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'the-license',
    heading: 'What the MIT license gives you',
    blocks: [
      'You may use VibeShield on any codebase — personal, commercial, public, or private — at no cost and without attribution obligations. You may modify it, fork it, recompile it with your own rules, and ship the result inside your company. You may quote its output in your own documentation or blog. The only substantive condition is that redistributed copies of the software itself keep the copyright and license notice.',
      'Your findings are yours. Scan output — JSON, SARIF, PR comments, badge images — carries no license restrictions from us; publish it, delete it, or keep it under NDA as your situation requires.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'no-warranty',
    heading: 'No warranty — stated plainly',
    blocks: [
      'The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose. In practice this means a few concrete things, none of them hidden:',
      {
        list: [
          'A clean scan is not a guarantee of security. The ruleset covers ~120 known AI-code failure modes across 8 languages; it does not cover the ones nobody has catalogued yet, and it is not a substitute for a human who reads the diff.',
          'The maintainers are not liable for losses arising from use of the tool — including the costs of a missed finding or a false-positive delay. This is the standard MIT limitation; we are stating it, not burying it.',
          'Release tags, rule-pack versions, and the Action are provided without an SLA. Support is community-first: GitHub issues, read by the people who write the rules.',
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'your-obligations',
    heading: 'What we ask you to do',
    blocks: [
      'The tool is only honest if its users are, so three asks:',
      {
        list: [
          'Treat findings as advice, not verdicts. Every finding carries a why and a suggested fix; a human who understands the code makes the accept/dismiss call. The dismiss flow writes an auditable reason precisely so the judgement is yours and provably yours later.',
          'Do not use the name, the shield logo, or the badge to imply endorsement by the maintainers or by any vendor VibeShield happens to scan. The badge states a scan result, not a relationship.',
          'If you redistribute a modified scanner, make clear it is a fork. Security tooling that silently diverges from its upstream helps nobody.',
        ],
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'trademarks',
    heading: 'Names and trademarks',
    blocks: [
      '“VibeShield” and the shield mark belong to this project and are used here only to describe it. Cursor, Copilot, Claude Code, Windsurf, Aider, Devin, Snyk, Socket, Semgrep, Dependabot, and Gitleaks are trademarks of their respective owners; when they appear on this site it is factual compatibility or comparison, never an endorsement in either direction.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'the-site',
    heading: 'This website',
    blocks: [
      'The vibeshield.dev site and its GitHub Pages deployment are informational and also MIT-licensed source. Docs and blog posts describe v1 behavior as we understand it at the time of writing; when code and documentation disagree, the code in the repository wins and we consider the docs buggy — tell us and we fix them.',
      'Privacy for this site and the product is governed by the privacy page, which we keep as short and honest as this one.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'changes',
    heading: 'How this document changes',
    blocks: [
      'If the project ever stops being free and open source (the maintainers see no reason it would), this page changes first and the license changes with it. For an MIT-licensed tool, “changes to these terms” is mostly a restatement of the license — so the honest summary is: the license in the repo is the deal, and this page is the human-readable translation of it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    id: 'contact',
    heading: 'Contact',
    blocks: [
      'Questions about licensing or redistribution: hi@vibeshield.dev. For anything about vulnerabilities in the tool itself, use security@vibeshield.dev instead — the disclosure policy on the security page explains why and how fast you get a reply.',
    ],
  },
];

const mitText = `Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy
of this software and associated documentation files (the "Software"), to deal
in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell
copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is
furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:

The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all
copies or substantial portions of the Software.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE
AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER
LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,
OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE
SOFTWARE.`;
---

<LegalDoc
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms of use for VibeShield, in clauses a human wrote: what the MIT license gives you, what a clean scan does not guarantee, and what the project asks in return."
  canonical="/terms"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Terms"
  updated="September 13, 2026"
  plainNote="VibeShield is free, MIT-licensed software. You can use it on anything, including closed commercial code. In exchange, the tool makes no promises it cannot keep — and neither do we. The binding text is the MIT license; this page is that text with the Latin removed."
  clauses={clauses}
  crossLink="/privacy"
  crossLabel="See also: Privacy"
>
  <div slot="tail">
    <h2 class="mt-4 text-[22px] font-semibold">The license text, verbatim</h2>
    <pre class="scroll-x fade-x mt-4 rounded-[var(--radius-card)] border border-[var(--color-hairline)] bg-[var(--color-elevated)] p-5 font-mono text-[13px] leading-[1.7] text-[var(--color-muted)]">MIT License

Copyright (c) 2026 VibeShield contributors

{mitText}</pre>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-faint)]">Source: <a class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline" href={`${SITE.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`}>{SITE.repo}/LICENSE</a>.</p>
  </div>
</LegalDoc>
